(arc lead-ins and lead-outs, G2 and G3)
(PureCutCNC reference program for the QtPlasmaC simulator check, issue #954.)
(Hand-written from the QtPlasmaC manual for LinuxCNC 2.9; each stanza names)
(the manual section it comes from. See ../README.md.)

(Manual: Preamble and Postamble Codes)
G21 G40 G49 G64 P0.1 G80 G90 G92.1 G94 G97
(Manual: Paused Motion)
M52 P1
(Manual: Automatic Material Handling - select, wait, then take the feed rate)
(from the material; the three codes must come in this order)
M190 P1
M66 P3 L3 Q1
F#<_hal[plasmac.cut-feed-rate]>

(A rounded rectangle with a hole. Every cut enters and leaves on a quarter)
(circle tangent to the path, so the pierce mark stays off the part edge.)

(hole: 40 mm, centre X70 Y50, counter-clockwise, 10 mm arc lead-in and lead-out)
G0 X80 Y40
M3 $0 S1
G3 X90 Y50 I0 J10
G3 X90 Y50 I-20 J0
G3 X80 Y60 I-10 J0
M5 $0

(outline: 100 x 60 with 10 mm corners, clockwise, 5 mm arc lead-in and lead-out)
G0 X15 Y45
M3 $0 S1
G3 X20 Y50 I0 J5
G1 X20 Y70
G2 X30 Y80 I10 J0
G1 X110 Y80
G2 X120 Y70 I0 J-10
G1 X120 Y30
G2 X110 Y20 I-10 J0
G1 X30 Y20
G2 X20 Y30 I0 J10
G1 X20 Y50
G3 X15 Y55 I-5 J0
M5 $0

(Manual: Preamble and Postamble Codes)
G0 X0 Y0
G21 G40 G49 G64 P0.1 G80 G90 G92.1 G94 G97
